course: dictionary
lesson: 15016
title: Words that ring and echo
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resonating means making a deep, clear sound that carries on and echoes. «The church bell was still resonating long after the last strike.» The words after the bell show the sound keeps going, so resonating must mean ringing on and echoing.
explain: In science, a guitar body or a glass can be resonating. It shakes strongly when a sound has the same note as it. «The guitar's wooden body was resonating when I played the low string.» The clue is that the body hums because the note matches it.
explain: Resonating can also mean that a message feels true to someone. «Her story was resonating with the children, who had all felt lonely too.» Try the swap: "her story was matching with the children" makes sense, so resonating with means it matches their feelings.
fact: Resonating is the -ing form of the verb resonate.
fact: «Resonating» can mean a deep sound that rings on and echoes.
fact: In science, something is resonating when it vibrates strongly because a sound matches it.
fact: «Resonating with» someone means a story or idea matches their own feelings or experience.
fact: Similar words like echoing, ringing and vibrating each fit some sentences better than others, so check the context.
exercise: «The bell's deep note was still resonating across the valley.» What is the bell's sound doing? | Falling silent at once | Turning into a whisper | Getting quieter and quieter | *Ringing and echoing on across the valley
exercise: «When the singer hit the high note, the glass started resonating on the table.» What does resonating mean in science here? | Breaking into pieces | Going cold to the touch | Changing colour | *Vibrating strongly because a sound matches it
exercise: «Her story was resonating with everyone in the class, who had felt lonely too.» What does resonating with mean? | Being too long to read | Ending the story early | *Matching their feelings, so it feels true | Making everyone angry
test: «The guitar body was resonating with the low note, so it hummed loudly.» What does resonating mean? | *Vibrating strongly to match the sound | Sinking into the table | Switching off | Playing a different tune
test: «The poem was resonating with Maya, who had moved far away from home too.» What does resonating with mean here? | Making her fall asleep | Stopping her from reading | *Feeling true and meaningful to her | Boring her completely
exam: «The choir's voices were resonating through the empty hall.» What does resonating mean? | Hiding in the corners | Fading away before anyone sang | Shrinking to nothing | *Echoing deeply through the space
